We Are:&nbsp;

RTB House is a next-generation performance demand-side platform (DSP) that uses proprietary Deep Learning AI algorithms to help brands grow. The company is the market leader in driving performance using Deep Learning across the entire purchase funnel.&nbsp;

Founded in 2012, and now operating in 90+ markets, RTB House has always been private-by-design. It embraces first-party advertising and a relentless approach to innovation. RTB House offers end-to-end Deep Learning-powered AdTech products and solutions to maximize conversion, drive new customer acquisition, create engagement, and fuel long-term demand for a global base of clients.

The Talent Acquisition Specialist will perform the full cycle recruitment for the company in EMEA region, and will manage the candidate experience throughout the process. The TAS will manage a variety of specialty recruitment systems ensuring that the company attracts, selects and retains highly talented individuals.

You will:&nbsp;

• generate a high quality pipeline of candidates by conducting interview calls daily;

• meet monthly individual recruitment goals;

• provide excellent service to the candidates;

• be fully responsible for attracting and sourcing highly talented company members;

• create and recommend recruitment strategies and approaches;

• proactively source, network and market job opportunities to build pipelines of qualified candidates and sell the advantages of working for RTB House;

• utilize existing tools and technology to source, evaluate, interview, and present qualified candidates to hiring managers for consideration;

• provide consistent communication to team members or business stakeholders on positions and recruitment strategies;

• seek, build, and maintain strong candidate relationships;

• work to build an understanding of the unique business and talent needs of each market;

• partner effectively with the Talent Acquisition team and other departments to achieve goals.

Desired experience:

• minimum 2 years of direct talent sourcing and recruitment experience (end-to-end);

• excellent networking abilities and communication skills;

• proactive and can-do attitude;

• excellent verbal, written and interpersonal communication skills at all levels and cultures of the organization;

• analytical approach to managing pipeline;

• demonstrated ability to work independently, manage competing priorities and meet deadlines;

• fluency in English is a must.

We Offer:&nbsp;

• A chance to cooperate in a truly international environment with the best people;

• Flexible work location;

• Possibility to learn in an international organisation in one of the fastest growing online advertising sectors;

• Friendly atmosphere while cooperation with a dynamic team of open minded professionals and passion for internet technology and advertising solutions;

• A dedicated annual budget for external training and language courses.

Apply now!&nbsp;

You don't need to tick every box to apply. If you are passionate about digital marketing, send us your CV, and we'll review it.

About WPP Media

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence, and world-class partnerships - all united by our pioneering agentic marketing platform, WPP Open - we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity, and deliver transformational growth. 

WPP Media is WPP's AI-driven media operating unit, bringing together media, data, and partnerships to deliver creative personalisation at scale. Connected through WPP Open and powered by Open Intelligence, clients see exactly where, how, and why their media investment is working.

For more information, visit wppmedia.com .

Role Summary and Impact &nbsp;

As a Trainee in Operations, you will support the GOAT team across social and influencer marketing projects, gaining hands-on experience in project coordination, campaign execution, stakeholder communication, and reporting. &nbsp;

• Work closely with the Operations team on social and influencer marketing campaigns, supporting day-to-day project coordination and execution.

• Collaborate with WPP partners and internal teams from planning through execution, delivery, and final reporting.

• Assist in campaign optimization by ensuring project information, budgets, timelines, and deliverables are accurately tracked and updated.

• Support GOAT Directors and Managers in managing influencer projects, including budgeting, KPI setting, implementation tracking, and performance reporting.

• Maintain accurate project records in internal systems, including budget phasing, campaign status, and key operational updates.

• Coordinate administrative requirements such as contracts, allocation management, paperwork processing, and compliance with client principles.

What You Will Learn &nbsp;

• Influencer marketing and social content brief analysis

• Influencer proposal structure and development process

• Influencer profile checking, rate card review, contract and PPW processing

• Creative idea brainstorming

• Reporting, data processing, and number-checking skills

• Communication, negotiation, teamwork, and problem-solving skills

Skills and Experience &nbsp;

• Fresh-graduated with major in Marketing, Business Administration, Communications,… and available for the minimum 6 months duration internship.&nbsp;

• Experience in advertising/communication/ influencer &amp; KOLs industry, especially as a project/account management role is a strong plus&nbsp;

• Good interpersonal skill, problem solving&nbsp;

• Good in communication: Master in Vietnamese (both speaking &amp; writing) &amp; Excellent in English (speaking, presenting &amp; writing)&nbsp;

• Good at MS office, proposal ppt, excel,…

• Passionate &amp; interested in influencer marketing

Life at WPP Media &amp; Benefits&nbsp; &nbsp;

Our passion for shaping the next era of media is powered by our commitment to   Be Extraordinary, investing in our employees to inspire transformational creativity. We also   Lead Optimistically,   firmly believing   in and   Championing Growth and Development   for every individual. This commitment allows WPP Media employees to   leverage   the extensive global WPP Media &amp; WPP networks to pursue their passions, build vital professional connections, and learn at the   cutting edge   of marketing and advertising.   &nbsp;

We   Create an Open environment   built on trust and respect, where everyone feels they belong and has opportunities to progress. This inclusive culture is fostered through a variety of employee resource groups and frequent in-office events   showcasing   team wins, sharing thought leadership, and celebrating holidays and milestone events. Our comprehensive benefits package reflects this commitment, including competitive medical, group retirement plans, vision, and dental insurance, significant paid time off, preferential partner discounts, and employee mental health awareness days.   &nbsp; &nbsp;

